      "full_text": "The Nyakyusa (also called the Sokile) are a Bantu ethnolinguistic group who live in the mountains of southern Mbeya Region of Tanzania and the Northern Region of Malawi. They speak the Nyakyusa language, a member of the Bantu language family.\n\n\n== Belief system ==\n\n\n=== God ===\n\nThe traditional god of the Nyakyusa people is called Kyala, which is the name for God in the Nyakyusa language.\n\n\n== See also ==\nList of ethnic groups in Tanzania\nHistory of Tanzania\nHistory of Malawi\n\n\n== References ==\n\nArnold, Bernd. (Steuer und Lohnarbeit im Südwesten von Deutsch-   Ostafrika,1891 bis 1916)\nBauer, Andreus. (Raising the Flag of War)\nCharsley, S.R.  (The Princes of Nyakyusa)\nEthnologue report: Nyakyusa\nIliffe, John.  (A Modern History of Tanganyika)\nMerensky, A.  (Deutsche Arbeit am Nyaßa)\nMwakikagile, Godfrey (Africa and the West)\nOliver, Roland. (Sir Harry Johnston & the Scramble for Africa)\nTew, Mary.  (Peoples of the Lake Nyasa Region)\nWilson, Monica.  (Good Company)"
